    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Hervé, je dois tout t'avouer.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Herve, I must confess everything.' Camille prepares to reveal the agency secret. The clause hinges on the everyday verb meaning 'must'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Vas-y, je suis en veille.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go ahead, I am on standby.' Herve tells her he is ready to listen. The clause hinges on the everyday verb meaning 'go ahead'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Tu connais notre client Philippe?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You know our client Philippe?' Camille brings up their mystery assignment. In everyday spoken French, rising intonation on 'know' at the end is enough to turn the sentence into a question.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Oui, notre fameux client mystérieux.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, our famous mysterious client.' Herve remembers the anonymous contract. The key noun here means 'client', anchored by its matching French article.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Philippe, en fait, c'est Mathias.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Philippe, in fact, is Mathias.' Camille delivers the shocking truth. A short, idiomatic conversational reply that keeps the exchange moving naturally.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Quoi? Ce n'est pas possible!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What? That is not possible!' Herve reacts with utter bewilderment. A short, idiomatic conversational reply that keeps the exchange moving naturally.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "C'est la pure vérité, Hervé.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is the pure truth, Herve.' Camille confirms that she is telling the truth. The adjective meaning 'pure' takes its feminine form here to match the noun it describes.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Mathias nous a engagés nous?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Mathias hired us?' Herve cannot believe their senior partner used them. This conversational past tense combines a helper verb with the past verb form for 'hired'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Il préparait son grand départ.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He was preparing his big departure.' Camille explains Mathias's secret motive. The verb meaning 'was preparing' pairs naturally with the noun for 'departure' in everyday conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Il nous a manipulés totalement!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He manipulated us completely!' Herve feels exploited by the deception. The clause hinges on the everyday verb meaning 'has'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Il avait confiance en nous.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'He had confidence in us.' Camille interprets Mathias's actions as a sign of trust. The verb meaning 'had' pairs naturally with the noun for 'confidence' in everyday conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Tout s'explique enfin maintenant.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything makes sense now.' Herve finally understands the strange clues. The clause hinges on the everyday verb meaning 'explains itself'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "camille",
      "t": "Nous devons garder le secret.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We must keep the secret.' Camille urges discretion between the two assistants. The verb meaning 'must' pairs naturally with the noun for 'secret' in everyday conversation.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "herve",
      "t": "Cette agence est complètement folle!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
